Z||000002||Sleeper||08-08-2001||02:31 AM||||and theres always West Coast Fiero too, about 10 to 15 north of LAX, thats if your flying in through there.<P>------------------<BR>85 GT Auto<BR>17" Racing Hart C5 wheels wrapped with Kumho Ecsta Supra 712 tires, Intrax lowering springs, KYB shocks, KYB-GR2 struts, West Coast Fiero Strut Tower Bar, West Coast Fiero Cold-Air Intake w/ HKS Super Flow filter, Beretta brake upgrade in front, KVS Performance Slotted Rotors in rear, Earl's Steel-Braided Brake Lines J.E.T. super chip and MSD Blaster Coil.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Songman||08-08-2001||03:08 AM||||Sqoach,<P>I don't know what your schedule is but every couple of years I like to fly to L.A. and rent a car and drive the Pacific Coast Highway from Malibu to Monterey. It is some of the most beautiful scenery you will ever see.. If you have time, I recommend it..<P>Check out Malibu, Santa Barbara, spend the night at Morro Bay, check out some of the trails down to some of the beaches (Jade Beach is my favorite), tour the Hearst Castle, take the 17 Mile Drive at Carmel and see the most beautiful golf course in the world.. as you can tell, I love it!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||14
